<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:32:default:default">
<!--
    kuna option bejoinpass high (the default), GH-904: a big-endian register
    pair a call hands back and the function returns untouched is one value.

    bejoin joins a function's returned pair by that function's own proof and
    a call's output pair by its callee's.  viahook calls through a function
    pointer, keeps the pair across ext(), and returns it; its caller usehook
    reads both words of the result, so bejoin callers proves viahook 64-bit,
    while the callee behind the pointer is unknown.  The RETURN joined high
    word first and the call first register low, so the same two registers
    printed swapped:
        unsigned long long v1; // v1:v0
        v1 = (*hook)();
        ext();
        return CONCAT44((int4)v1,(int4)((uint8)v1 >> 0x20));      (bug)
    A call whose two registers reach a RETURN joined high word first,
    untouched in the same places, now joins high word first too, so the
    function returns the call's value as it came.

    The other direction, an unproven wrapper of a proven callee, needs the
    callee's recovered prototype, which only a whole-binary decompile-all
    states (protoorder); tests/cli/bejoinpass-*.json cover it on the same
    images.

    Stage: P4 calls and prototypes (output-prototype), option bejoinpass.
    Pass 1 is the default (high), pass 2 option bejoinpass off.

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoinpass_mips32_O2
    (gcc -O2, MIPS o32) and bejoinpass_ppc32_O2.o (clang -O2, PowerPC), both
    from bejoinpass.c; see bejoinpass.provenance.

    Assert #1: the default returns the call's value on both targets.
    Assert #2: the default joins the call high word first (v0:v1, r3:r4).
    Assert #3: off prints the swap on both targets.
    Assert #4: off joins the call first register low (v1:v0, r4:r3).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">03e0000800000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoinpass_mips32_O2</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu viahook</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option bejoinpass off</com>
  <com>lo fu viahook</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoinpass_ppc32_O2.o</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>option bejoinpass high</com>
  <com>lo fu viahook</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option bejoinpass off</com>
  <com>lo fu viahook</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="bejoinpass #1: the default returns the call's value as it came" min="2" max="2">^\s*return v1;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="bejoinpass #2: the default joins the call's pair high word first" min="2" max="2">unsigned long long v1; // (v0:v1|r3:r4)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="bejoinpass #3: off prints the pair with its halves swapped" min="2" max="2">return CONCAT44\(\(int4\)v1,\(int4\)\(\(uint8\)v1 &gt;&gt; 0x20\)\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="bejoinpass #4: off joins the call's pair first register low" min="2" max="2">unsigned long long v1; // (v1:v0|r4:r3)$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
